// All database READS used by pages live here (TODO 29). Pages never talk to Prisma directly.
//
// Every function is cached ("use cache") so the pages stay fast and can still be prepared
// ahead of time, EXCEPT searchContent (its input is whatever a visitor types, so caching it
// would fill the cache with one entry per search; it only runs inside the dynamic /search part)
// and getMySocialLikes (it is about ONE logged-in person, so it must never go into the shared cache).
// When something is saved to the database later (Phase 2), the code that saves it must also
// call updateTag("<tag>") so the pages show the new data. The tags are:
//   "communities"  -> the list of communities, their rules and member counts
//   "posts"        -> post lists, vote totals and comment counts (Home, Popular, c/<slug>, post)
//   "comments"     -> the comment thread under one post
//   "modlog"       -> the public moderation log (every moderator action must update it)
//   "ads"          -> the pool of running ads (code that approves, pauses or ends an ad must update it)
// A new comment changes BOTH the thread and the count on the post: update "comments" and "posts".
// A vote on a post updates "posts"; a vote on a comment updates "comments".
// These caches are shared by everybody, so they hold NO personal data. The highlighted arrow
// (the logged-in person's own vote) is loaded separately: src/app/vote/my-votes.ts and
// src/components/MyVotesProvider.tsx. The same goes for the filled heart on a Social post
// (the person's own like): getMySocialLikes below, called by the page for each request.
//
// Return plain data only (text, numbers, lists), never Prisma objects or Dates.
